---
wide: true
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Mushroom encyclopedia"
description: "Mushrooms without myths: a catalog of edible, poisonous and medicinal species, reviews of human clinical research and supplement safety — linked to primary sources."
og_type: "website"
permalink: "/en/"
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero__aurora" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="hero__blob hero__blob--a"></span>
    <span class="hero__blob hero__blob--b"></span>
    <span class="hero__blob hero__blob--c"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="hero__gills" aria-hidden="true">
    <svg viewBox="-300 -300 600 600" width="600" height="600">
      <g stroke="var(--color-leaf)" stroke-width="0.6" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.5">
        {% for i in range(0, 36) %}
          {% set angle = (loop.index0 / 36) * 360 %}
          <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="280" y2="0" transform="rotate({{ angle }})"/>
        {% endfor %}
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <p class="hero__eyebrow">Mushrooms and evidence-based science</p>
  <h1 class="hero__title">Mushroom World</h1>
  <p class="hero__lead">
    What is actually known about mushrooms: which species are edible and
    which are dangerous, what human clinical trials have shown, and what
    to know before buying supplements.
  </p>
  <p class="hero__note">
    Every entry is built on peer-reviewed work and links to the primary
    source. No miracle promises — only what the data supports.
  </p>
  <div class="hero__actions">
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ '/en/griby/' | url }}">Mushroom catalog</a>
    <a class="btn" href="{{ '/en/sezon/' | url }}">What to gather when</a>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="stats" aria-label="Site in numbers">
  <a class="stat" href="{{ '/en/griby/' | url }}"><span class="stat__num" data-counter="{{ collections.gribyEn.length }}">{{ collections.gribyEn.length }}</span><span class="stat__label">species in the catalog</span></a>
  <a class="stat" href="{{ '/griby/' | url }}"><span class="stat__num">{{ collections.griby.length }}</span><span class="stat__label">species in the Russian version</span></a>
</div>

<section aria-labelledby="species" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
  <h2 id="species" style="font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">From the catalog</h2>
  <div class="species-strip">
    {% set shown = 0 %}
    {% for g in collections.gribyEn %}
      {% if g.data.image and shown < 14 %}
        {% set shown = shown + 1 %}
        <a class="species-chip" href="{{ g.url | url }}">
          <img src="{{ g.data.image | url }}" alt="{{ g.data.title }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          <span class="species-chip__body">
            <span class="species-chip__name">{{ g.data.title }}</span>
            <span class="species-chip__latin">{{ g.data.latin_name }}</span>
          </span>
        </a>
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p style="margin-top: var(--space-2);"><a href="{{ '/en/griby/' | url }}">Full catalog →</a></p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="about-short" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
  <h2 id="about-short" style="font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">About the project</h2>
  <p style="max-width: 640px; color: var(--color-text-muted);">
    Mushroom World is an independent reference about fungi. We collect
    and adapt open material, base entries on peer-reviewed publications,
    and present them in a readable form. Articles and research reviews
    are currently available in Russian; the species catalog and the
    seasonal calendar are being translated.
  </p>
  <p style="margin-top: var(--space-3);">
    <a href="{{ '/en/o-proekte/' | url }}">More about the project →</a>
  </p>
</section>
